  {
   "line": 7,
   "text": "So let the filter listen to itself, reusing its own output, two samples back. That feedback puts poles just inside the rim, beside the zeros. Divide by the distance to each pole. From fifteen hundred hertz, the zero and the pole look equally far, so they cancel. [surprise-oh] Ninety-seven percent. The whine still sits on its zero. That's a notch.",
